{
  "title": "Distal Humerus Physeal Separation - Pediatric",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4006/distal-humerus-physeal-separation--pediatric",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Oct 27 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Distal Humerus Physeal Seperations are traumatic fractures usually seen in children under the age of three and are often associated with child abuse.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be made with plain radiographs of the elbow.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually operative closed reduction and percutaneous pinning",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**typically seen in children under the age of 3**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "although variations can be seen in older children (see below)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mechanism",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**vaginal delivery (birth fracture)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "from force of labor or obstetric maneuvers",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "shoulder dystocia and traumatic delivery are at higher risk",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "cesarean section",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "from excessive traction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**nonaccidental trauma**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "rotational force / twisting",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "fall on outstretched hand with elbow extended",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pathoanatomy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "physis is biomechanically the weakest location in distal humerus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "it is also referred to as a **transphyseal distal humerus fracture**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "abuse or **battered child syndrome (up to 50%)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Salter-Harris classification",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "older children (>3y) have Salter-Harris II injuries",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "metaphyseal fragment attached to distal fragment",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "younger children (<3y) have Salter-Harris I injuries",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "pure physeal injury",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "rare cases have intra-articular extension (Salter-Harris III or IV)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "can be difficult to differentiate from a lateral condyle fracture",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Displacement of the distal fragment",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**most commonly posteromedial**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "rarely can be anterior",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "birthing process (see above)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "fall from height (bed, chair, down stairs) typically onto extended elbow",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "another child jumps/falls on a child's elbow",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**nonaccidental trauma**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "unwitnessed injuries",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "inconsistent explanations",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "history of multiple injuries, burns, bites, bruising",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "skin lesions are most common findings in nonaccidental trauma",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inspection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "pseudoparalysis / diminished spontaneous movement",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "swelling or ecchymosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "neurovascular",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "rarely neurovascular compromise",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP and lateral centered on the elbow",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "\"baby gram\"",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "(radiograph of entire extremity) or forearm/arm radiographs can lead to missed diagnosis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "stress radiographs",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "may be helpful to clarify the diagnosis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "skeletal survey",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "if child abuse suspected",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**posteromedial displacement of the radial and ulnar shafts** relative to the distal humerus",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4006/images/img_2100.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4006/images/img_2099.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "may be the only finding in infants",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**forearm not aligned with humeral shaft**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**soft tissue swelling**, joint effusion (posterior fat pad)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "anterior fat pad may be absent",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "if capitellar ossification center is present, it will be aligned with radius shaft, making diagnosis definitive",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ultrasound",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "uncertain diagnosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "advantage",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "no need for sedation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "disadvantage",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "needs experienced technician",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "static exam",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "detect separation of epiphysis from metaphysis by noting lack of cartilage at distal humeral metaphysis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "dynamic exam",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "detect instability of epiphysis relative to metaphysis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "not routinely used",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "disadvantage",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "requires sedation in young children",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Elbow arthrography",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "uncertain diagnosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "often combined with CRPP in OR",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "visualization of entire distal articular surface and proximal radius",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "posterolateral approach or direct posterior approach",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "direct posterior into olecranon fossa recommended in young children to prevent iatrogenic damage to the articular cartilage when posterolateral portal is used",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "inject equal parts saline:contrast",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "bring elbow through range of motion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "if pinning is needed, arthrogram aids visualization of **pin starting points on capitellum**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "aids assessment of quality of reduction by **seeing anterior humeral line intersecting capitellum**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "advantage",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "if performed under anesthesia in OR, can perform reduction and stabilization simultaneously if needed",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Elbow dislocation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "almost never happens in <3 yrs because distal humerus physis is weaker than bone-ligament interface, predisposing to physeal fracture rather than ligament disruption/dislocation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "typically distal fragment is displaced posterolaterally with elbow dislocations",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Other fractures",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "often misdiagnosed (or delayed diagnosis up to 1 week) as supracondylar, condyle, epicondyle fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "posterior long arm splint then long arm casting x 2-3 weeks",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "limited role because most fractures are **displaced**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**nondisplaced fractures**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**late presenting fractures**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "treat nonoperatively initially",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "deformity will persist/develop, requiring osteotomy in future",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "closed reduction and pinning",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**displaced fractures** (most)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "pinning is necessary to ensure adequate reduction, which may be lost with casting alone once the swelling subsides",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**combined with elbow arthrogram** to determine direction of initial displacement and adequate reduction",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technique",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Closed Reduction and Pinning**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "general anesthesia",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "use elbow arthrogram to determine direction of displacement",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "reduction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "maneuver",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "gentle traction (very little force required)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "distal fragment may sometimes be grasped between index finger and thumb and reduced to humeral shaft",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "correction of translation/malrotation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "elbow flexion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "acceptable parameters (similar to supracondylar humerus fractures)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "no cubitus varus",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**anterior humeral line should bisect capitellum**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "no malrotation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pinning",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "2 or 3 x 0.062inch K wires",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "these larger pins help prevent loss of reduction",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "from lateral side, retrograde fashion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "divergent",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "engage both cortices",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "good spread at fracture site",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "then perform live fluoroscopy through range of motion and slight varus/valgus stress to ensure no loss of reduction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "immobilization",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "bend / cut pins",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "splint the arm",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "postoperative care",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "admit overnight to observe for compartment syndrome (may not be necessary in all cases)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "see 1 week postoperatively with radiographs to ensure no loss of reduction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "see 3 weeks postoperatively with radiographs and remove pins in office",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "allow full active ROM at that time",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "physical therapy is rarely needed",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "typically follow patients for 2-4 years after injury to ensure there is no growth arrest, deformity, or osteonecrosis (see below)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Cubitus varus**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**up to 70% have this complication**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**more common than with supracondylar fractures**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "cause",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AVN of medial condyle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "malunion (common because of missed diagnosis, or loss of reduction)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "growth arrest",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "treatment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**lateral closing wedge osteotomy**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Medial or lateral condyle AVN**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "may lead to fishtail deformity seen in all distal humerus fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Loss of motion**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually no functional limitation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Growth disturbance**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "progressive cubitus varus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "joint irregularities",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "angular deformity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "limb-length discrepancy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "treatment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**observe initially, undertake surgery when > 5 years old**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**larger extremity**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**child more cooperative**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "can address all deformities in one surgery.",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Often missed diagnosis** as very difficult to diagnose",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "up to 50% missed by radiologist",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In patients with early recognition and prompt treatment, outcomes are very good",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
